    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0746" n="736" xml:id="pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/2–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-01T13:00:00+08:00">February 1, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 1—7:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>341. Unconfirmed rumor but coming from reliable source indicates that Central
                    Bank was ordered by the Minister of Finance<anchor n="9" xml:id="d688-f1"/> to
                    release unlimited gold yuan currency to purchase commodities through large
                    Chinese firms and Central Trust for shipment to southern ports. Purpose is to
                    keep commodities out of hands of Communists and leave them gold yuan currency.
                    Result locally has been an increase of local prices from 200 to 300 percent
                    during 3–day Chinese New Year holiday. Gold yuan currency January 28 quoted at
                    320 to 1 US; quote today is 700 to 1 and gold bars advanced from gold yuan
                    15,000 per ounce to gold yuan 43,000 during same period.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 341, repeated Nanking 260.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d688-f1" n="9" xml:id="d688-f1-content">
